- How would you extend to handle k up to n with space-saving tricks?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a DP variant transforming flips into max-sum of k disjoint subarrays on a simple gain array.

## Key Concepts
- DP with two matrices: dp for best total, best for segments ending at i
- Transform 0/1 to +1/-1 gains to linearize gains
- Reconstructing segments via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesAfterKFlips(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const gain = Array.from({length:n}, (_,i)=> s[i]==='0'?1:-1);
  const NEG = -1e9;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const best = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      best[i][t] = Math.max(best[i-1][t] + gain[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + gain[i-1]);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], best[i][t]);
    }
  }
  const ones = s.split('').filter(c=>c==='1').length;
  return ones + dp[n][k];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over time with multiple constraints: multiple transactions, reconstruction, and edge-case handling.

## Key Concepts
- Two DP states: cash (not holding) and hold (holding).
- Transitions model buy/sell with transaction count t.
- Base cases initialize day 0; backtracking recovers trade days.
- Space optimization possible to O(k) with rolling arrays.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxProfit(prices, k){
  const n = prices.length;
  if (n===0 || k===0) return 0;
  const cash = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const hold = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) cash[0][t] = (t===0)?0:-1e15;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    for (let t=0; t<=k; t++){
      cash[i][t] = cash[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) cash[i][t] = Math.max(cash[i][t], hold[i-1][t] + prices[i-1]);
      hold[i][t] = hold[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) hold[i][t] = Math.max(hold[i][t], cash[i-1][t-1] - prices[i-1]);
    }
  }
  let best = 0;
  for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) best = Math.max(best, cash[n][t]);
  return best;
}
```

